      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nCommission may determine expiry of collective bargaining notice\n\n(5) If the Commission is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the period provided for in subparagraph (3)(c)(i) is not\nappropriate in all the circumstances; and\n\n(b) another period, ending no later than the end of the period of\n10 years beginning on the day the corporation gave the\ncollective bargaining notice, is appropriate in all the\ncircumstances;\nthe Commission may give to the corporation a written notice\ndetermining that other period for the purposes of\nsubparagraph (3)(c)(ii).\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nCommission may determine expiry of collective bargaining notice\n\n(5) If the Commission is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the period provided for in subparagraph (3)(c)(i) is not\nappropriate in all the circumstances; and\n\n(b) another period, ending no later than the end of the period of\n10 years beginning on the day the corporation gave the\ncollective bargaining notice, is appropriate in all the\ncircumstances;\nthe Commission may give to the corporation a written notice\ndetermining that other period for the purposes of\nsubparagraph (3)(c)(ii).\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-20-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-20-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "67bc75c342f3bd8287635b58d59183496495e2e8b0d49619faf8c216810b751a",
      "skos:note": "Commission may determine expiry of collective bargaining notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 At the end of section 93AD",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nCommission may determine expiry of collective bargaining notice\n\n(5) If the Commission is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the period provided for in subparagraph (3)(c)(i) is not\nappropriate in all the circumstances; and\n\n(b) another period, ending no later than the end of the period of\n10 years beginning on the day the corporation gave the\ncollective bargaining notice, is appropriate in all the\ncircumstances;\nthe Commission may give to the corporation a written notice\ndetermining that other period for the purposes of\nsubparagraph (3)(c)(ii).\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions"
    },
