    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-95ab-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95AB(4) Commission may withdraw the benefit of class exemption in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-95ab-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The notice under subsection (1):\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the Commission gives the person\nthe notice; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earliest of the following times:\n\n(i) if the Tribunal sets it aside under subsection 102(5G)—\nat the end of the day on which the Tribunal sets it aside;\n\n(ii) if the Commission revokes the notice—when it is\nrevoked;\n\n(iii) the time the determination under section 95AA ceases to\nbe in force.\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The notice under subsection (1):\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the Commission gives the person\nthe notice; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earliest of the following times:\n\n(i) if the Tribunal sets it aside under subsection 102(5G)—\nat the end of the day on which the Tribunal sets it aside;\n\n(ii) if the Commission revokes the notice—when it is\nrevoked;\n\n(iii) the time the determination under section 95AA ceases to\nbe in force.\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-95ab"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-95ab-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "067538b0ed501684fe8fac100f07cf47404d4d7e6bad20df4eea23af08be051b",
      "skos:note": "Commission may withdraw the benefit of class exemption notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-95ab-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95AB(4) Commission may withdraw the benefit of class exemption in",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The notice under subsection (1):\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the Commission gives the person\nthe notice; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earliest of the following times:\n\n(i) if the Tribunal sets it aside under subsection 102(5G)—\nat the end of the day on which the Tribunal sets it aside;\n\n(ii) if the Commission revokes the notice—when it is\nrevoked;\n\n(iii) the time the determination under section 95AA ceases to\nbe in force.\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions"
    },
