    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 After subsection 102(5)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(5AAA) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93(3B):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat the corporation or other person on whom the conditions\nrelating to the conduct or proposed conduct have been\nimposed has not failed to comply with those conditions—the\nTribunal must make a determination setting aside the notice;\nor\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.\n\n(5AAB) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93AAA(1):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\n(i) apart from section 93AAA, the Commission would not\nhave had grounds referred to in\nsubparagraph 93AAA(1)(b)(i); or\n\n(ii) compliance with the conditions imposed by the notice\nwould not ensure those grounds would not exist;\n\nthe Tribunal must make a determination setting aside the\nnotice; or\n\nAuthorisations, notifications and class exemptions  Schedule 9\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(5AAA) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93(3B):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat the corporation or other person on whom the conditions\nrelating to the conduct or proposed conduct have been\nimposed has not failed to comply with those conditions—the\nTribunal must make a determination setting aside the notice;\nor\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.\n\n(5AAB) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93AAA(1):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\n(i) apart from section 93AAA, the Commission would not\nhave had grounds referred to in\nsubparagraph 93AAA(1)(b)(i); or\n\n(ii) compliance with the conditions imposed by the notice\nwould not ensure those grounds would not exist;\n\nthe Tribunal must make a determination setting aside the\nnotice; or\n\nAuthorisations, notifications and class exemptions  Schedule 9\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-24-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-24-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d8f9d91b308d3390733f4763d7f5648c3b6e5d3be9ddbdadd8f1655db737865",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal must make a determination setting aside the notice if conditions are not met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 After subsection 102(5)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(5AAA) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93(3B):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat the corporation or other person on whom the conditions\nrelating to the conduct or proposed conduct have been\nimposed has not failed to comply with those conditions—the\nTribunal must make a determination setting aside the notice;\nor\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.\n\n(5AAB) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93AAA(1):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\n(i) apart from section 93AAA, the Commission would not\nhave had grounds referred to in\nsubparagraph 93AAA(1)(b)(i); or\n\n(ii) compliance with the conditions imposed by the notice\nwould not ensure those grounds would not exist;\n\nthe Tribunal must make a determination setting aside the\nnotice; or\n\nAuthorisations, notifications and class exemptions  Schedule 9\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice."
    },
