    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 After subsection 102(5C)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(5D) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93ACA(1):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\n(i) apart from section 93ACA, the Commission would not\nhave had grounds referred to in\nsubparagraph 93ACA(1)(b)(i); or\n\n(ii) compliance with the conditions imposed by the notice\nwould not ensure those grounds would not exist;\n\nthe Tribunal must make a determination setting aside the\nnotice; or\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.\n\n(5E) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93AD(5):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(5D) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93ACA(1):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\n(i) apart from section 93ACA, the Commission would not\nhave had grounds referred to in\nsubparagraph 93ACA(1)(b)(i); or\n\n(ii) compliance with the conditions imposed by the notice\nwould not ensure those grounds would not exist;\n\nthe Tribunal must make a determination setting aside the\nnotice; or\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.\n\n(5E) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93AD(5):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-26-ss-5d"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-26-ss-5e"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 After subsection 102(5C)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(5D) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93ACA(1):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\n(i) apart from section 93ACA, the Commission would not\nhave had grounds referred to in\nsubparagraph 93ACA(1)(b)(i); or\n\n(ii) compliance with the conditions imposed by the notice\nwould not ensure those grounds would not exist;\n\nthe Tribunal must make a determination setting aside the\nnotice; or\n\n(b) if the person who applied for the review does not so satisfy\nthe Tribunal—the Tribunal must make a determination\naffirming the notice.\n\n(5E) Upon a review of the giving of a notice by the Commission under\nsubsection 93AD(5):\n\n(a) if the person who applied for the review satisfies the Tribunal\nthat:\n\nSchedule 9  Authorisations, notifications and class exemptions"
    },
