      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) any submissions that are received within the period specified under paragraph (2)(b);"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "within",
      "cml:logicSummary": "after considering specified factors within a period",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) any information received under paragraph 90(6)(b) or (c) (as that paragraph applies because of subsection (2A) of this section) within the period specified in the notice mentioned in that paragraph;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-ss-3-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "need not",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Commission need not take into account submissions or information received after end of periods",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) any information obtained from consultations under paragraph 90(6)(d) (as that paragraph applies because of subsection (2A) of this section)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92(4) Subsections 91A(3) to (5)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-92-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission must not make a determination varying an\nauthorisation in relation to conduct unless the Commission is\nsatisfied in all the circumstances that:\n\n(a) if, in making the determination to grant the authorisation in\nrelation to conduct, the Commission was satisfied that the\nconduct would not have the effect, or would not be likely to\nhave the effect, of substantially lessening competition—the\nvariation would not have the effect, or would not be likely to\nhave the effect, of increasing the extent to which the conduct\nlessens competition; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—the variation would not\nresult, or would not be likely to result, in a reduction in the\nextent to which the benefit to the public of the authorisation\noutweighs any detriment to the public caused by the\nauthorisation.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The Commission must not make a determination varying an\nauthorisation in relation to conduct unless the Commission is\nsatisfied in all the circumstances that:\n\n(a) if, in making the determination to grant the authorisation in\nrelation to conduct, the Commission was satisfied that the\nconduct would not have the effect, or would not be likely to\nhave the effect, of substantially lessening competition—the\nvariation would not have the effect, or would not be likely to\nhave the effect, of increasing the extent to which the conduct\nlessens competition; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—the variation would not\nresult, or would not be likely to result, in a reduction in the\nextent to which the benefit to the public of the authorisation\noutweighs any detriment to the public caused by the\nauthorisation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99226666f902d5eed1a9157d6ad169f0d4d5cf78c9433100a2caa25260f6a347",
      "skos:note": "Commission cannot make a determination varying an authorisation in relation to conduct unless certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-92-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92(4) Subsections 91A(3) to (5)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Commission must not make a determination varying an\nauthorisation in relation to conduct unless the Commission is\nsatisfied in all the circumstances that:\n\n(a) if, in making the determination to grant the authorisation in\nrelation to conduct, the Commission was satisfied that the\nconduct would not have the effect, or would not be likely to\nhave the effect, of substantially lessening competition—the\nvariation would not have the effect, or would not be likely to\nhave the effect, of increasing the extent to which the conduct\nlessens competition; or\n\n(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply—the variation would not\nresult, or would not be likely to result, in a reduction in the\nextent to which the benefit to the public of the authorisation\noutweighs any detriment to the public caused by the\nauthorisation."
    },
