    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92 Providing false or misleading information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-92-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not give information to the Commission or Tribunal\nunder this Division or Part IX in connection with any of the\nfollowing if the person is negligent as to whether the information is\nfalse or misleading in a material particular:\n\n(a) an application for a merger authorisation;\n\n(b) an application for a minor variation of a merger\nauthorisation;\n\n(c) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of a merger authorisation;\n\nAuthorisations, notifications and class exemptions  Schedule 9\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(d) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of a merger authorisation and the substitution of\nanother merger authorisation;\n\n(e) a review of a determination in relation to an application or\nproposal referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d).\nNote:\nUnder section 76, the Court may order a person who contravenes this\nsection to pay a pecuniary penalty. See also sections 80AC, 81A and\n86C for other related remedies.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), proof that the person knew, or\nwas reckless as to whether, the information was false or misleading\nin a material particular is taken to be proof that the person was\nnegligent as to whether the information was false or misleading in\na material particular.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person must not give information to the Commission or Tribunal\nunder this Division or Part IX in connection with any of the\nfollowing if the person is negligent as to whether the information is\nfalse or misleading in a material particular:\n\n(a) an application for a merger authorisation;\n\n(b) an application for a minor variation of a merger\nauthorisation;\n\n(c) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of a merger authorisation;\n\nAuthorisations, notifications and class exemptions  Schedule 9\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(d) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of a merger authorisation and the substitution of\nanother merger authorisation;\n\n(e) a review of a determination in relation to an application or\nproposal referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d).\nNote:\nUnder section 76, the Court may order a person who contravenes this\nsection to pay a pecuniary penalty. See also sections 80AC, 81A and\n86C for other related remedies.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), proof that the person knew, or\nwas reckless as to whether, the information was false or misleading\nin a material particular is taken to be proof that the person was\nnegligent as to whether the information was false or misleading in\na material particular.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-92-2-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "97f6ca8850d7fa7d6d54ed02be079b38c518e2bbb695ba41f6ab9ead1e10acc7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-92-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92 Providing false or misleading information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not give information to the Commission or Tribunal\nunder this Division or Part IX in connection with any of the\nfollowing if the person is negligent as to whether the information is\nfalse or misleading in a material particular:\n\n(a) an application for a merger authorisation;\n\n(b) an application for a minor variation of a merger\nauthorisation;\n\n(c) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of a merger authorisation;\n\nAuthorisations, notifications and class exemptions  Schedule 9\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(d) an application for, or the Commission’s proposal for, the\nrevocation of a merger authorisation and the substitution of\nanother merger authorisation;\n\n(e) a review of a determination in relation to an application or\nproposal referred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d).\nNote:\nUnder section 76, the Court may order a person who contravenes this\nsection to pay a pecuniary penalty. See also sections 80AC, 81A and\n86C for other related remedies.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), proof that the person knew, or\nwas reckless as to whether, the information was false or misleading\nin a material particular is taken to be proof that the person was\nnegligent as to whether the information was false or misleading in\na material particular."
    },
