    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-106a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "106A Issue of apparatus licence taken to be an acquisition of an",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-106a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.79",
      "values:originalText": "asset and conduct\n\n(1) For the purposes of the provisions of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 mentioned in subsection (2), the issue of an\napparatus licence to a person is taken to be:\n\n(a) an acquisition by the person of an asset of another person;\nand\n\n(b) conduct engaged in by the person.\n\n(2) The provisions of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 are:\n\n(a) section 50 and subsection 81(1); and\n\n(b) Parts VII and IX, to the extent that those provisions relate to\nsection 50 of that Act.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a transmitter licence issued under\nsection 102 or to an NBS transmitter licence.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) does not apply to the issue of an apparatus licence if\nthe licence is issued under Division 7 by way of renewal of an\nexisting apparatus licence.",
      "skos:definition": "asset and conduct\n\n(1) For the purposes of the provisions of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 mentioned in subsection (2), the issue of an\napparatus licence to a person is taken to be:\n\n(a) an acquisition by the person of an asset of another person;\nand\n\n(b) conduct engaged in by the person.\n\n(2) The provisions of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 are:\n\n(a) section 50 and subsection 81(1); and\n\n(b) Parts VII and IX, to the extent that those provisions relate to\nsection 50 of that Act.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a transmitter licence issued under\nsection 102 or to an NBS transmitter licence.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) does not apply to the issue of an apparatus licence if\nthe licence is issued under Division 7 by way of renewal of an\nexisting apparatus licence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-106a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-106a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-106a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-106a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8062d09a512866640dd2e7c65ab1f75710e7b13f70112470aafcd3860a9aa051"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-9-sec-106a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "106A Issue of apparatus licence taken to be an acquisition of an",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 79,
      "values:originalText": "asset and conduct\n\n(1) For the purposes of the provisions of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 mentioned in subsection (2), the issue of an\napparatus licence to a person is taken to be:\n\n(a) an acquisition by the person of an asset of another person;\nand\n\n(b) conduct engaged in by the person.\n\n(2) The provisions of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 are:\n\n(a) section 50 and subsection 81(1); and\n\n(b) Parts VII and IX, to the extent that those provisions relate to\nsection 50 of that Act.\n\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a transmitter licence issued under\nsection 102 or to an NBS transmitter licence.\n\n(4) Subsection (1) does not apply to the issue of an apparatus licence if\nthe licence is issued under Division 7 by way of renewal of an\nexisting apparatus licence."
    },
    {
