    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-10-sec-83",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "83 Findings and admissions of fact in proceedings to be evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-10-sec-83"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In a proceeding against a person under section 82 or in an\napplication under subsection 51ADB(1) or 87(1A) for an order\nagainst a person, a finding of any fact made by a court, or an\nadmission of any fact made by the person, is prima facie evidence\nof that fact if the finding or admission is made in proceedings:\n\n(a) that are proceedings:\n\n(i) under section 77, 80, 81, 86C, 86D or 86E; or\n\n(ii) for an offence against section 44ZZRF or 44ZZRG; and\n\n(b) in which that person has been found to have contravened, or\nto have been involved in a contravention of, a provision of\nPart IV or IVB, or of section 55B, 60C or 60K.\n\n(2) The finding or admission may be proved by production of:\n\n(a) in any case—a document under the seal of the court from\nwhich the finding or admission appears; or\n\n(b) in the case of an admission—a document from which the\nadmission appears that is filed in the court.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In a proceeding against a person under section 82 or in an\napplication under subsection 51ADB(1) or 87(1A) for an order\nagainst a person, a finding of any fact made by a court, or an\nadmission of any fact made by the person, is prima facie evidence\nof that fact if the finding or admission is made in proceedings:\n\n(a) that are proceedings:\n\n(i) under section 77, 80, 81, 86C, 86D or 86E; or\n\n(ii) for an offence against section 44ZZRF or 44ZZRG; and\n\n(b) in which that person has been found to have contravened, or\nto have been involved in a contravention of, a provision of\nPart IV or IVB, or of section 55B, 60C or 60K.\n\n(2) The finding or admission may be proved by production of:\n\n(a) in any case—a document under the seal of the court from\nwhich the finding or admission appears; or\n\n(b) in the case of an admission—a document from which the\nadmission appears that is filed in the court.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-10-sec-83-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-10-sec-83-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5bb9d6ab8775622389fbdf6640b31b13feb0730f591ec0f96cb66b621ca788f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-10-sec-83",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "83 Findings and admissions of fact in proceedings to be evidence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 81,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In a proceeding against a person under section 82 or in an\napplication under subsection 51ADB(1) or 87(1A) for an order\nagainst a person, a finding of any fact made by a court, or an\nadmission of any fact made by the person, is prima facie evidence\nof that fact if the finding or admission is made in proceedings:\n\n(a) that are proceedings:\n\n(i) under section 77, 80, 81, 86C, 86D or 86E; or\n\n(ii) for an offence against section 44ZZRF or 44ZZRG; and\n\n(b) in which that person has been found to have contravened, or\nto have been involved in a contravention of, a provision of\nPart IV or IVB, or of section 55B, 60C or 60K.\n\n(2) The finding or admission may be proved by production of:\n\n(a) in any case—a document under the seal of the court from\nwhich the finding or admission appears; or\n\n(b) in the case of an admission—a document from which the\nadmission appears that is filed in the court."
    },
