      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the matter must be a matter\nthat:\n\n(a) constitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) Division 4A or 4B of Part 3.3 of the\nRadiocommunications Act 1992; or\n\n(iii) any of the terms of an undertaking under section 87B of\nthis Act or under section 218 of the Australian\nConsumer Law; or\n\n(b) is relevant to:\n\n(i) a designated communications matter (as defined by\nsubsection (9) of this section); or\n\n(ii) a designated water matter (as defined by\nsubsection (9A) of this section); or\n\n(iii) the making of a decision by the Commission under\nsubsection 90(1) in relation to an application for a\nmerger authorisation; or\n\n(iv) the making of a decision by the Commission under\nsubsection 91B(4), 91C(4), 93(3) or (3A) or 93AC(1) or\n(2).",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the matter must be a matter\nthat:\n\n(a) constitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) Division 4A or 4B of Part 3.3 of the\nRadiocommunications Act 1992; or\n\n(iii) any of the terms of an undertaking under section 87B of\nthis Act or under section 218 of the Australian\nConsumer Law; or\n\n(b) is relevant to:\n\n(i) a designated communications matter (as defined by\nsubsection (9) of this section); or\n\n(ii) a designated water matter (as defined by\nsubsection (9A) of this section); or\n\n(iii) the making of a decision by the Commission under\nsubsection 90(1) in relation to an application for a\nmerger authorisation; or\n\n(iv) the making of a decision by the Commission under\nsubsection 91B(4), 91C(4), 93(3) or (3A) or 93AC(1) or\n(2).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "93c52d89a64b5c333e59f7b447f620aaad97b60d813d30d9ae3846eae119dbc0",
      "skos:note": "Matter must be a matter that constitutes or may constitute a contravention of the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-11-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 After subsection 155(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the matter must be a matter\nthat:\n\n(a) constitutes, or may constitute, a contravention of:\n\n(i) this Act; or\n\n(ii) Division 4A or 4B of Part 3.3 of the\nRadiocommunications Act 1992; or\n\n(iii) any of the terms of an undertaking under section 87B of\nthis Act or under section 218 of the Australian\nConsumer Law; or\n\n(b) is relevant to:\n\n(i) a designated communications matter (as defined by\nsubsection (9) of this section); or\n\n(ii) a designated water matter (as defined by\nsubsection (9A) of this section); or\n\n(iii) the making of a decision by the Commission under\nsubsection 90(1) in relation to an application for a\nmerger authorisation; or\n\n(iv) the making of a decision by the Commission under\nsubsection 91B(4), 91C(4), 93(3) or (3A) or 93AC(1) or\n(2)."
    },
