    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 After subsection 155(5A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-11-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\nPower to obtain information, documents and evidence  Schedule 11\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(5B) Paragraph (5)(a) does not apply to the extent that:\n\n(a) the notice relates to producing documents; and\n\n(b) the person proves that, after a reasonable search, the person is\nnot aware of the documents; and\n\n(c) the person provides a written response to the notice,\nincluding a description of the scope and limitations of the\nsearch.\nNote:\nA defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (5B)(b) (see section 13.4 of the Criminal Code).\n\n(6) For the purposes of (but without limiting) paragraph (5B)(b), a\ndetermination of whether a search is reasonable may take into\naccount the following:\n\n(a) the nature and complexity of the matter to which the notice\nrelates;\n\n(b) the number of documents involved;\n\n(c) the ease and cost of retrieving a document relative to the\nresources of the person who was given the notice;\n\n(d) any other relevant matter.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\nPower to obtain information, documents and evidence  Schedule 11\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(5B) Paragraph (5)(a) does not apply to the extent that:\n\n(a) the notice relates to producing documents; and\n\n(b) the person proves that, after a reasonable search, the person is\nnot aware of the documents; and\n\n(c) the person provides a written response to the notice,\nincluding a description of the scope and limitations of the\nsearch.\nNote:\nA defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (5B)(b) (see section 13.4 of the Criminal Code).\n\n(6) For the purposes of (but without limiting) paragraph (5B)(b), a\ndetermination of whether a search is reasonable may take into\naccount the following:\n\n(a) the nature and complexity of the matter to which the notice\nrelates;\n\n(b) the number of documents involved;\n\n(c) the ease and cost of retrieving a document relative to the\nresources of the person who was given the notice;\n\n(d) any other relevant matter.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-3-ss-5b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-3-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e92084ca29b735ebbfcafa1524480700dc0209cba833ec56965d7631f451e105"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-11-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 After subsection 155(5A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\nPower to obtain information, documents and evidence  Schedule 11\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\n(5B) Paragraph (5)(a) does not apply to the extent that:\n\n(a) the notice relates to producing documents; and\n\n(b) the person proves that, after a reasonable search, the person is\nnot aware of the documents; and\n\n(c) the person provides a written response to the notice,\nincluding a description of the scope and limitations of the\nsearch.\nNote:\nA defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (5B)(b) (see section 13.4 of the Criminal Code).\n\n(6) For the purposes of (but without limiting) paragraph (5B)(b), a\ndetermination of whether a search is reasonable may take into\naccount the following:\n\n(a) the nature and complexity of the matter to which the notice\nrelates;\n\n(b) the number of documents involved;\n\n(c) the ease and cost of retrieving a document relative to the\nresources of the person who was given the notice;\n\n(d) any other relevant matter."
    },
    {
