          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-3-ss-5b-logic-alleninterval-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7cdaa628f66145178cefcd9809f18fada9b56c6ba6759b14e11b1a62665bc38e",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from duty to produce documents under certain circumstances.",
      "dc:description": "Written response including scope and limitations of search."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-11-sec-3-ss-5b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3(5B) After subsection 155(5A)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(5B) Paragraph (5)(a) does not apply to the extent that:\n\n(a) the notice relates to producing documents; and\n\n(b) the person proves that, after a reasonable search, the person is\nnot aware of the documents; and\n\n(c) the person provides a written response to the notice,\nincluding a description of the scope and limitations of the\nsearch.\nNote:\nA defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in\nparagraph (5B)(b) (see section 13.4 of the Criminal Code)."
    },
