      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.83",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a notice issued under subsection 155(1) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 was in force immediately before the\ncommencement of this item, after that commencement:\n\n(a) the notice continues in force; and\n\n(b) section 155 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 as\namended by this Act applies in relation to the notice;\nas if the notice had been issued under that section as so amended.\n(2)\nHowever, the amendment of subsection 155(6A) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 made by this Schedule does not apply in relation to\na notice served before the commencement of this item.\n\nSchedule 12  Access to services",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nIf a notice issued under subsection 155(1) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 was in force immediately before the\ncommencement of this item, after that commencement:\n\n(a) the notice continues in force; and\n\n(b) section 155 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 as\namended by this Act applies in relation to the notice;\nas if the notice had been issued under that section as so amended.\n(2)\nHowever, the amendment of subsection 155(6A) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 made by this Schedule does not apply in relation to\na notice served before the commencement of this item.\n\nSchedule 12  Access to services",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-11-sec-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e576a65835e97942d3c412b5c9ab61c0b6c985248e3e3a519f1abe219d353613",
      "skos:note": "Continuation of existing notices under subsection 155(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-11-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Existing section 155 notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 83,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nIf a notice issued under subsection 155(1) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 was in force immediately before the\ncommencement of this item, after that commencement:\n\n(a) the notice continues in force; and\n\n(b) section 155 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 as\namended by this Act applies in relation to the notice;\nas if the notice had been issued under that section as so amended.\n(2)\nHowever, the amendment of subsection 155(6A) of the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010 made by this Schedule does not apply in relation to\na notice served before the commencement of this item.\n\nSchedule 12  Access to services"
    },
