        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b):"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPart",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Facility capacity is considered in relation to its expanded capacity.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) if the facility is currently at capacity, and it is reasonably possible to expand that capacity,"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Facility expansion costs are considered in relation to its expanded capacity.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) without limiting paragraph (1)(b), the cost referred to in that paragraph includes all costs associated with having multiple users of the facility (including such costs that would be incurred if the service is declared)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-2-logic-argumentation-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Facility expansion consideration implies a duty to consider its expanded capacity.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b):"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44CA(3) Meaning of declaration criteria",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting the matters to which the Council may have regard\nfor the purposes of section 44G, or the designated Minister may\nhave regard for the purposes of section 44H, in considering\nwhether paragraph (1)(d) of this section applies the Council or\ndesignated Minister must have regard to:\n\n(a) the effect that declaring the service would have on\ninvestment in:\n\n(i) infrastructure services; and\n\n(ii) markets that depend on access to the service; and\n\n(b) the administrative and compliance costs that would be\nincurred by the provider of the service if the service is\ndeclared.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Without limiting the matters to which the Council may have regard\nfor the purposes of section 44G, or the designated Minister may\nhave regard for the purposes of section 44H, in considering\nwhether paragraph (1)(d) of this section applies the Council or\ndesignated Minister must have regard to:\n\n(a) the effect that declaring the service would have on\ninvestment in:\n\n(i) infrastructure services; and\n\n(ii) markets that depend on access to the service; and\n\n(b) the administrative and compliance costs that would be\nincurred by the provider of the service if the service is\ndeclared.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "688cc72cca4815cbc8c3d7cb0df814fec8b25a66dc57e8a5d8b94fd093dcc4f6",
      "skos:note": "Council must have regard to the effect of declaring the service on investment and administrative costs."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44CA(3) Meaning of declaration criteria",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Without limiting the matters to which the Council may have regard\nfor the purposes of section 44G, or the designated Minister may\nhave regard for the purposes of section 44H, in considering\nwhether paragraph (1)(d) of this section applies the Council or\ndesignated Minister must have regard to:\n\n(a) the effect that declaring the service would have on\ninvestment in:\n\n(i) infrastructure services; and\n\n(ii) markets that depend on access to the service; and\n\n(b) the administrative and compliance costs that would be\nincurred by the provider of the service if the service is\ndeclared."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-44ca-ss-3-norm",
