    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-20-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20(3) After Subdivision C of Division 2A of Part IIIA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-12-sec-20-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Any of the following may make a written application to the\nCouncil asking it to recommend that the Commonwealth Minister\nrevoke the decision:\n\n(a) a person who is seeking access to the service;\n\n(b) the responsible Minister for the State or Territory;\n\n(c) the provider of the service.\n\nAccess to services  Schedule 12\nEffective access regimes  Part 2\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\nThe Council must give a copy of the application to each entity\nmentioned in paragraph (b) or (c), unless that entity is the\napplicant.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Any of the following may make a written application to the\nCouncil asking it to recommend that the Commonwealth Minister\nrevoke the decision:\n\n(a) a person who is seeking access to the service;\n\n(b) the responsible Minister for the State or Territory;\n\n(c) the provider of the service.\n\nAccess to services  Schedule 12\nEffective access regimes  Part 2\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\nThe Council must give a copy of the application to each entity\nmentioned in paragraph (b) or (c), unless that entity is the\napplicant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-20-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-20-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "596d3abb5d5cee774a77008601df08510e4231cdb694946d91bdcd7df875002f",
      "skos:note": "Any of the following may make a written application to the Council asking it to recommend that the Commonwealth Minister revoke the decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-12-sec-20-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20(3) After Subdivision C of Division 2A of Part IIIA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Any of the following may make a written application to the\nCouncil asking it to recommend that the Commonwealth Minister\nrevoke the decision:\n\n(a) a person who is seeking access to the service;\n\n(b) the responsible Minister for the State or Territory;\n\n(c) the provider of the service.\n\nAccess to services  Schedule 12\nEffective access regimes  Part 2\n\nNo. 114, 2017\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review)\nAct 2017\n\nThe Council must give a copy of the application to each entity\nmentioned in paragraph (b) or (c), unless that entity is the\napplicant."
    },
