      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the Council is not so satisfied, the Council must, in writing,\nrecommend to the Commonwealth Minister that he or she not\nrevoke the decision.\nNote 1:\nThere are time limits that apply to the Council’s recommendation: see\nsection 44NC.\nNote 2:\nThe Council may request information and invite public submissions:\nsee sections 44NBB and 44NE.\nNote 3:\nThe Council must publish its recommendation: see section 44NF.\n44NBB  Council may request information",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If the Council is not so satisfied, the Council must, in writing,\nrecommend to the Commonwealth Minister that he or she not\nrevoke the decision.\nNote 1:\nThere are time limits that apply to the Council’s recommendation: see\nsection 44NC.\nNote 2:\nThe Council may request information and invite public submissions:\nsee sections 44NBB and 44NE.\nNote 3:\nThe Council must publish its recommendation: see section 44NF.\n44NBB  Council may request information",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-12-sec-20"
      },
