    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "185(4) Merger clearances and authorisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-13-sec-185-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "(4) At and after the commencement time, Part IX as amended by\nSchedule 9 to the amending Act applies in relation to a\ndetermination (a clearance determination) made by the\nCommission before, at or after the commencement time under\nformer section 95AM in relation to a clearance, as if the clearance\ndetermination related to a merger authorisation that is not an\noverseas merger authorisation.\nNote:\nFormer section 95AM is repealed by Schedule 9 to the amending Act,\nbut has a continued limited application: see subsection (2).\nOld law continues to apply to review of merger clearance\ndeterminations if proceedings are pending at commencement",
      "skos:definition": "(4) At and after the commencement time, Part IX as amended by\nSchedule 9 to the amending Act applies in relation to a\ndetermination (a clearance determination) made by the\nCommission before, at or after the commencement time under\nformer section 95AM in relation to a clearance, as if the clearance\ndetermination related to a merger authorisation that is not an\noverseas merger authorisation.\nNote:\nFormer section 95AM is repealed by Schedule 9 to the amending Act,\nbut has a continued limited application: see subsection (2).\nOld law continues to apply to review of merger clearance\ndeterminations if proceedings are pending at commencement",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c182d9e2624b24bf3972c647bea199972e4e9126f97a75c417c1061ab0cba2fb",
      "skos:note": "Conditional application of amended Part IX to clearance determinations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-13-sec-185-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "185(4) Merger clearances and authorisations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "(4) At and after the commencement time, Part IX as amended by\nSchedule 9 to the amending Act applies in relation to a\ndetermination (a clearance determination) made by the\nCommission before, at or after the commencement time under\nformer section 95AM in relation to a clearance, as if the clearance\ndetermination related to a merger authorisation that is not an\noverseas merger authorisation.\nNote:\nFormer section 95AM is repealed by Schedule 9 to the amending Act,\nbut has a continued limited application: see subsection (2).\nOld law continues to apply to review of merger clearance\ndeterminations if proceedings are pending at commencement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
