      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "185(5) Merger clearances and authorisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-13-sec-185-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, if:\n\n(a) an application for a review of a clearance determination is\nmade under former Division 3 of Part IX before the\ncommencement time; and\n\n(b) the Tribunal has not made its decision on the review before\nthe commencement time;\nthen:\n\n(c) subsection (4) does not apply in relation to the clearance\ndetermination; and\n\n(d) despite the repeal of that Division by Schedule 9 to the\namending Act, that Division continues to apply in relation to\nthe clearance determination at and after the commencement\ntime, as if the repeal had not happened.\nOld law merger clearances and authorisations granted or coming\ninto force after commencement to be treated as new law merger\nauthorisations",
      "skos:definition": "(5) However, if:\n\n(a) an application for a review of a clearance determination is\nmade under former Division 3 of Part IX before the\ncommencement time; and\n\n(b) the Tribunal has not made its decision on the review before\nthe commencement time;\nthen:\n\n(c) subsection (4) does not apply in relation to the clearance\ndetermination; and\n\n(d) despite the repeal of that Division by Schedule 9 to the\namending Act, that Division continues to apply in relation to\nthe clearance determination at and after the commencement\ntime, as if the repeal had not happened.\nOld law merger clearances and authorisations granted or coming\ninto force after commencement to be treated as new law merger\nauthorisations",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-13-sec-185-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f80fccb86ac1f4e70962a6510253dde7be2b6db8ca531966fea6cf898aa7feae",
      "skos:note": "Conditional exemption from subsection (4) for clearance determinations made before commencement time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017#sch-13-sec-185-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "185(5) Merger clearances and authorisations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, if:\n\n(a) an application for a review of a clearance determination is\nmade under former Division 3 of Part IX before the\ncommencement time; and\n\n(b) the Tribunal has not made its decision on the review before\nthe commencement time;\nthen:\n\n(c) subsection (4) does not apply in relation to the clearance\ndetermination; and\n\n(d) despite the repeal of that Division by Schedule 9 to the\namending Act, that Division continues to apply in relation to\nthe clearance determination at and after the commencement\ntime, as if the repeal had not happened.\nOld law merger clearances and authorisations granted or coming\ninto force after commencement to be treated as new law merger\nauthorisations"
    },
